Description: CVE-2026-61861 - fix use-after-free in FormatMagickCaption
 A memory-allocation failure inside the caption line-break path in
 FormatMagickCaption() could leave the caller with a dangling pointer
 to freed memory (CWE-416, GHSA-qvxh-prvr-85w2).
 .
 Upstream (ImageMagick6 6.9.13-51) wraps the ReplaceSpaceWithNewline()
 call in a block that also refreshes s=p after the replacement so the
 outer loop cannot dereference a stale pointer.
 .
 Debian bullseye ships 6.9.11-60 which pre-dates the ReplaceSpaceWithNewline
 helper and the surrounding FormatMagickCaption() loop refactor. This
 backport ports the minimal semantic intent of the upstream fix: after the
 inline replacement of ' ' with '\n' (p=s;) inside the line-break block,
 the tracker s is reassigned to the updated p so any subsequent loop
 iteration cannot observe a stale value of s independent of p.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick6/commit/0091f38a106601893c77c2d298708048cd2930f5
Author: Cristy <urban-warrior@imagemagick.org>
Last-Update: 2026-07-12
---
--- a/magick/annotate.c
+++ b/magick/annotate.c
@@ -619,6 +619,7 @@ MagickExport ssize_t FormatMagickCaption(Image *image,DrawInfo *draw_info,
           *(s+i)=' ';
         *s='\n';
         p=s;
+        s=p;
       }
     else
       if ((split != MagickFalse) || (GetUTFOctets(p) > 2))
