@@ -0,0 +1,65 @@
+# CVE-2026-56372 — Not Affected (Debian 11 ImageMagick 6.9.11.60)
+
+| Field | Value |
+|-------|-------|
+| **CVE** | CVE-2026-56372 |
+| **Component** | `MagnifyImage()` pixel-art scaler |
+| **Upstream file** | `MagickCore/resize.c` (ImageMagick 7.x) |
+| **Package** | imagemagick 8:6.9.11.60+dfsg-1.3+deb11u16 |
+| **Assessment** | **Not affected** — vulnerable code path absent in 6.x |
+| **Fixed upstream in** | 7.1.2-19 |
+
+---
+
+## Summary
+
+The upstream fix (commit `8f6b59383ce65d839ad3e2aa578d5d7a7dd1d0ec`) changes the
+default initialisers of the `magnification` and `width` locals in
+`MagnifyImage()` from `(1,1)` to `(2,3)`, so that an unrecognised
+`-define magnify:method=<name>` falls back safely to the Scale2X path.
+
+Without that fallback, a misconfigured `magnify:method` leaves
+`magnification = 1` and `width = 1` while the surrounding loop still performs a
+2x/3x expansion, producing out-of-bounds pixel access.
+
+## Why Debian 11 is not affected
+
+Debian 11 (bullseye) ships ImageMagick 6.9.11.60, where `MagnifyImage()` lives
+in `magick/resize.c` and is a materially different implementation: a hard-coded
+2x pixel-art scaler with no configurable method dispatch. Specifically it has:
+
+* no `magnification` local
+* no `width` local
+* no `scaling_method` local and no switch over pixel-art methods
+* no `GetImageArtifact()` / `GetImageOption()` lookup for `magnify:method`
+* a fixed 3x3 virtual-pixel window with a `2*columns` by `2*rows` `CloneImage()`
+
+A whole-tree grep confirms that `magnify:method` appears only in the bundled
+HTML documentation (`www/command-line-options.html`, `www/defines.html`) and
+never as a source-level artifact or option lookup. No Debian-carried patch in
+`debian/patches/` reintroduces the configurable dispatch.
+
+Because the vulnerable configurable-dispatch path does not exist in the 6.x
+`MagnifyImage()`, CVE-2026-56372 is not reachable on this codebase and no
+functional source change is required.
+
+## Recommended action
+
+Mark as not affected rather than patching:
+
+```json
+{
+  "vulnerability": "CVE-2026-56372",
+  "products": [
+    "pkg:deb/debian/imagemagick"
+  ],
+  "status": "not_affected",
+  "justification": "vulnerable_code_not_present"
+}
+```
+
+## References
+
+* Upstream advisory: https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-8vfj-q2cp-5m5j
+* Upstream fix: https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/8f6b59383ce65d839ad3e2aa578d5d7a7dd1d0ec
+* Debian Security Tracker: https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-56372
